From bdc360e1f5fa898afa5ba3865a9190f59554f072 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kimwin2 <kimwin3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 05:22:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] feat(spec-decode): add DDTreeProposer scaffold on top of
 DFlash
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds an optional DDTree (Diffusion Draft Tree) extension to the dflash
spec-decode path. When `speculative_config.ddtree_enabled` is false
(default), the runtime is identical to upstream PR #41703 — the new
proposer class is never imported or instantiated.

When enabled, `DDTreeProposer(DFlashProposer)` is constructed in place
of `DFlashProposer` and builds a top-k draft tree from per-position
logits using ported MIT primitives from liranringel/ddtree (build,
compile, follow). C1 path returns the linear top-1 of the tree so the
token result is bit-identical to dflash; C2 (target-side tree verify)
is stubbed for the next iteration.

Adds:
* vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_utils.py — ported MIT primitives.
* vllm/v1/spec_decode/ddtree_proposer.py — DDTreeProposer subclass.
* SpeculativeConfig.ddtree_enabled / ddtree_budget / use_ddtree().
* gpu_model_runner branch to instantiate the new proposer.

Reference: Ringel & Romano, "Accelerating Speculative Decoding with
Block Diffusion Draft Trees", arXiv:2604.12989, 2026.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
